From 4a05ba3b467bc531bdcfa56a132c9b85f6b2dbd6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harry Lasry <harrylasry@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:35:50 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] 3DO: audio CD support

The 3DO core now asks for the block format of each read (READ command byte
7): 2048 bytes of user data, or 2352/2336/2340-byte raw blocks, with 96
subcode bytes on request. Main_MiSTer sends:
- CD-DA sectors with big-endian samples, as the 3DO expects (BIN and WAVE
  tracks are byte-swapped, MOTOROLA and CHD audio are not);
- raw data sectors, with a sync pattern and header for 2048-byte images;
- the Q subcode (track, index, relative and absolute times, CRC);
- the TOC control byte with ADR 1 (0x14 data, 0x10 audio) and the CUE FLAGS.
The READ address is always MSF: byte 4 is the top byte of the block count.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
